  <h1> The Exagerated GAS prices in Portugal </h1>
  <h3> This is still a real problem, and the portuguese population across the border decided to fuel the car in Spain gas stations </h3>
  <p> Due to the Middle East conflict the prices of gas have been <b> rising nonstop </b>, all over the world. Confronted with this kind of economic crisis, the population across the border decided to fuel its vehicles in Spain, because the price is lower. <p>
  <h2> The hell over Portugal: Protests </h2>
  <p> There are occuring several protests against the taxes on gas, and there were even hundreds of truck driver´s that organized a slow march on the autoway this weekend, which caused trafic troubles.
   <hr>
    <blockquote> Honestly I don´t understand what is the government´s problem on lowering the taxes over fuel. I know that they won´t be able to rob more money if they do that, but they should, finally, do something for the people that work so hard to fill their pockets... <footer> - <b><i>Arlindo Maia</i></b>, one of the truck drivers that are participating on the protest.</footer> <blockquote>
